      "writtenOn": "2023-08-09T08:51:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "request.onServiceFound and clientInfo.onServiceFound would always be called together right ?\n\nIn that case how about moving the call to request.onServiceFound inside clientInfo.onServiceFound ? This avoids forgetting to call one of the two, and it would be more consistent with onDiscoverServicesStarted and onStopDiscoverySucceeded, which already do metrics tracking (otherwise incrementing the counters and sending the metrics is done in 2 different places, which is harder to track).\n\nSame for onServiceLost",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1215,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 1215,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "914e3a5ae87268d1f24308fd12fd749820d8331c",
